# Playwright TypeScript Framework

TypeScript + Playwright automation framework with 5-agent pipeline for test development.

## Quick Start

``bash
# Setup
npm install && npx playwright install
cp config/environments/.env.example config/environments/.env.local  # Edit with your credentials

# Run tests
npm test                    # All tests
npm run test:chrome         # Chrome only
npm run test:headed         # Visible browser
npm run test:debug          # Debug mode

# Reports
npm run report              # Playwright HTML report
npm run allure:generate && npm run allure:open
``

## Agent Pipeline

| Agent | Invoke | Purpose |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Requirements | `@playwright-requirements` | Capture intent -> REQUIREMENTS.md + queue |
| Planner | `@playwright-test-planner` | Explore app -> test cases + selectors |
| Generator | `@playwright-test-generator` | Create .spec.ts files |
| Healer | `@playwright-test-healer` | Fix failing tests |
| Audit | `@playwright-pipeline-audit` | Compliance reports |

## Project Structure

``
src/
  pages/       # Page objects (extend BasePage)
  selectors/   # Centralized selectors (index.ts)
  utils/       # Helpers (logger, common-methods)
  data/        # Data adapters (Excel, JSON, DB)
  security/    # Vault (AES-256-GCM encryption)
  integrations/# External integrations (SharePoint)
  framework-contracts/ # Type definitions
  index.ts     # Barrel export

dist/          # Compiled framework (tsc output)

tests/
  setup/       # fixtures.ts, global setup
  specs/       # Test files by module
  examples/    # Pattern examples for agents

specs_planning/
  test-cases/  # Test case docs
  test-plans/  # Technical plans
  agent-queue.json
``

## Writing Tests

``typescript
import { test, expect } from '../../setup/fixtures';

test('should login', async ({ loginPage, config }) => {
  expect(await loginPage.login(config.admin_username, config.admin_password)).toBe(true);
});
``

## Fixtures

| Fixture | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `page` | Playwright page |
| `config` | Environment config (.env) |
| `loginPage` | Login page object |
| `homePage` | Home page object |
| `commonMethods` | Utility methods |

## Adding Page Objects

1. Add selectors to `src/selectors/index.ts`
2. Create `src/pages/{name}.page.ts` extending `BasePage`
3. Add fixture to `tests/setup/fixtures.ts`
4. Export from `src/pages/index.ts`

## Environment

``env
BASE_URL=https://your-app.com
HOME_URL=https://your-app.com/home
ADMIN_USERNAME=user
ADMIN_PASSWORD=pass
MFA_SECRET=YOUR_BASE32_SECRET
``

Switch environments: `CI_ENV=staging npm test`

## Commands

``bash
npm run typecheck           # TypeScript validation
npx playwright test --grep @smoke  # Run tagged tests
npm run clean               # Clear reports/logs
npm run build               # Compile src/ ? dist/
npm run build:clean         # Clean + rebuild
npm run client:package      # Package client deliverable
npm run lint:testcases      # Lint test case markdown
npm run pipeline:validate   # Full validation (sync + lint)
npm run sync:mistakes       # Inject rules into agent files
``

